{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "CBMZColumn",
    "description": "The WRF-Chem chem_opt = 170 gas-phase chemistry column: CBM-Z lifted over the 59-layer column, with the column processes WRF-Chem adds to each gas -- emissions, dry deposition through the ground and large-scale wet scavenging -- summed into one instantaneous tendency per species and layer. It is the document PLAN.md 1.4b scoped as 'the next coupling step' (CBM-Z is a 0-D reaction system; the column lifts it beside vertmx, Wesely, Madronich, emissions and wet deposition).\n\nWHAT IS MOUNTED. CBMZ (the 139-reaction system of components/gaschem/cbmz/cbmz.esm, by a reaction_systems ref) and CBMZRateConstants, closed by the shared peroxy-pool coupling library; the emissions_driver assembly of couplings/emissions_column.esm (EmissionsColumn and its four schemes, wired by the same two coupling libraries that document imports); Wesely's surface resistance and deposition velocity over all 65 gas slots of chem_opt 170 (row 2 of their per-gas tables), followed by dry_dep_driver's CBM-Z velocity reassignments (cbmz_velocity_assignment.esm); and wetdep_ls on a species axis of one, sulf. CBMZColumn holds the column: the 66 gases as [lev] states in molec/cm^3 and the column and surface fields each process reads.\n\nHOW CBM-Z IS LIFTED. The reaction system is 0-D. operator_compose(CBMZColumn, CBMZ), with one translate entry per species, merges each species' column tendency into its mass-action tendency, and composing a 0-D system with [lev] tendencies lifts it pointwise (esm-spec 10.5, 10.7): every reaction runs layer by layer, and its rate constants are lifted with it through pointwise variable_maps of T, M_air and the ten Madronich photolysis frequencies. CBMZColumn is systems[0], so its [lev] spelling survives the merge, and its observeds d<X>_dt = D(X) are the summed tendency. j_n2o5 is left at zero, which is what WRF hands CBM-Z under phot_opt = 1 (FORTRAN_BUGS B28). HCl and NH3 are constant reservoirs of the gas-phase mechanism (their identity reactions are removed), so the column carries them as its own states, moved only by emissions and deposition, and hands their values to the mechanism.\n\nUNITS AND GEOMETRY. KPP integrates molec/cm^3; every other WRF-Chem process works in ppmv. conv = 1e-6 dens2con_a rho, formed as the generated KPP interface forms it, is the one place the two meet: an emissions_driver tendency [ppmv/s] enters as conv d<x>_dt, and wetdep_ls's sulf removal as conv dc_dt (its concentrations are bare ppmv, which its gates require). Dry deposition needs no conversion: it is the flux vd X out of the lowest layer divided by that layer's thickness, vertmx's lower-boundary term with the mixing off. All processes of one model step read the same column geometry z_at_w and the same density (checked on every dumped step). The one Wesely input that reads the chemistry, the high-ammonia flag (NH3 > 2 SO2 in the lowest layer), is formed from the column's own state.\n\nWHAT IS NOT HERE. Vertical mixing (vertmx): the species-axis component (components/gaschem/chem_transport/chem_vertical_mixing.esm, lowered by EarthSciDiscretizations' tracer flux-boundary rule, PR #53) is on main but not mounted here yet; when it is, the deposition term becomes its flux boundary condition. Madronich is not computed here: the j-values are inputs (the KPP dump's jv), because couplings/madronich_column.esm closes the radiative transfer only for a cloud-free call and returns RADM2's channels on its own RT grid; wiring its j_col into this column is the next step. MOSAIC's gas-particle exchange of HNO3, HCl, NH3 and H2SO4 is not coupled here.\n\nTESTS. A separate capture with every one of these processes on at once (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_full.sh: emissions, Gunther, wetdep_ls with cu_physics = 0 so that WSM6 rains, Wesely), at five steps: local noon, an evening shower twice, midnight and the second morning. The column state is CBM-Z's at KPP entry, and every expected value is the SUM at that one state of each process's instantaneous tendency, each from a real64 replay of the Fortran at that state (data/eqwefic/chem170_full/replay_column.py): Vdot of cbmz_mosaic_Fun; the emissions_driver increment over dt; vertmx with K = 0 extrapolated to dt -> 0; wetdep_ls's increment over dt. All 66 species at all 59 layers are asserted (tools/fill_cbmz_column_tests.py). Measured: above the lowest layer the column reproduces the sum to 4.4e-12 relative at worst; in the lowest layer to 9e-7 of the total, which is the Wesely velocity's single precision (the replayed vertmx reads WRF's real32 ddvel, the column forms it in double through the Wesely components, whose own tests compare at rel 1e-5), so each assertion's absolute bound is 1e-5 of its layer's deposition term.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "chem_opt-170",
      "cbm-z",
      "column",
      "coupling"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Mass layers of the column, WRF kte."
    },
    "NSLOT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 65,
      "description": "Gas slots of chem_opt 170, numgas = 65 (slot 1 the dummy)."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "CBMZRateConstants": {
      "ref": "../components/gaschem/cbmz/cbmz_rate_constants.esm"
    },
    "EmissionsColumn": {
      "ref": "./emissions_column.esm",
      "model": "EmissionsColumn"
    },
    "Bio": {
      "ref": "../components/emissions/wrf_chem/gunther_biogenic.esm"
    },
    "BioCbmz": {
      "ref": "../components/emissions/wrf_chem/gunther_to_cbmz.esm"
    },
    "Anthro": {
      "ref": "../components/emissions/wrf_chem/cbmz_anthropogenic.esm"
    },
    "Aer": {
      "ref": "../components/emissions/wrf_chem/mosaic_anthropogenic.esm"
    },
    "WeselyRc": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wesely/surface_resistance.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NSPEC": "NSLOT"
      },
      "index_set_rename": {
        "spc": "slot"
      }
    },
    "WeselyVd": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wesely/deposition_velocity.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NSPEC": "NSLOT"
      },
      "index_set_rename": {
        "spc": "slot"
      }
    },
    "DryDep": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wesely/cbmz_velocity_assignment.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NSPEC": "NSLOT"
      },
      "index_set_rename": {
        "spc": "slot"
      }
    },
    "WetDep": {
      "ref": "../components/atmospheric_deposition/wrf_wetdep_ls/wetdep_ls.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "NLEV": "NLEV",
        "NSPEC": 1,
        "NGAS": 1
      }
    },
